          "quality": 0.04040404040404041,
          "answer": "VA life insurance offers financial security for Veterans, service members, and their spouses and dependent children. You can explore your options, manage your policy, and file claims to get the insurance benefits you've earned [S1].\n\nTo determine which life insurance program you may be eligible for, consider the following options:\n\n1. **Servicemembers Group Life Insurance (SGLI)**: Provides group life insurance while you're serving.\n2. **Family Servicemembers Group Life Insurance (FSGLI)**: Adds coverage for your spouse and dependent children.\n3. **Traumatic Injury Protection (TSGLI)**: Offers short-term financial support to help you recover from a severe injury.\n4. **Veterans Group Life Insurance (VGLI)**: Provides group life insurance once you've ended your service.\n5. **Service-Disabled Veterans Insurance (S-DVI)**: If you're disabled because of an injury or illness caused or made worse by your active service, you can continue your life insurance beyond 2 years after you leave the military.\n6. **Veterans Mortgage Life Insurance (VMLI)**: If you have a severe service-connected disability, this mortgage protection insurance can help your family pay off the home mortgage on a home that's been adapted to meet your needs [S5].\n\nIf you are a service-disabled Veteran, you may be eligible for **Service-Disabled Veterans Life Insurance (S-DVI)**, which provides low-cost coverage. To apply for S-DVI, you must meet specific requirements, including having a service-connected disability and being in good health except for any service-connected conditions [S3].\n\nFor managing your policy, you can access your VA life insurance policy online to check your policy's status, pay your premium, update your beneficiary, and more [S4].\n\nIf you become totally disabled or terminally ill, you may be eligible for certain benefit options, such as a waiver of premiums or accelerated benefits [S6].\n\nFor more information or assistance, you can contact the VA Life Insurance Center at 800-669-8477 [S3]."
        },
