          "prefill_tokens": 118,
          "quality": 0.039735099337748346,
          "answer": "VA life insurance offers various options for Veterans, service members, and their families. Here are the key points and actions you can take:\n\n1. **Determine Eligibility and Choose a Program**:\n   - **Servicemembers Group Life Insurance (SGLI)**: Provides group life insurance for active service members.\n   - **Family Servicemembers Group Life Insurance (FSGLI)**: Adds coverage for a service member\u2019s spouse and dependent children.\n   - **Traumatic Injury Protection (TSGLI)**: Offers short-term financial support after a severe injury.\n   - **Veterans Group Life Insurance (VGLI)**: Available to Veterans after they leave the military.\n   - **Service-Disabled Veterans Insurance (S-DVI)**: For Veterans with a service-connected disability.\n   - **Veterans Mortgage Life Insurance (VMLI)**: Mortgage protection for Veterans with severe service-connected disabilities who receive a Specially Adapted Housing (SAH) grant [S2].\n\n2. **Access and Manage Your Policy Online**:\n   - Use the VA or Prudential Insurance Company of America portals to check your policy status, pay premiums, update beneficiaries, and review renewal options [S3].\n\n3. **Special Circumstances**:\n   - **Totally Disabled Policyholders**: You may qualify for a **waiver of premiums** if you are totally disabled and meet specific conditions (e.g., disability occurs before age 65 and lasts at least 6 months). Apply using **VA Form 29-357** [S1].\n   - **Terminally Ill Policyholders**: You may receive **accelerated benefits** (up to 50% of the face value of your policy) if you or your spouse has a terminal illness with a prognosis of 9 months or less. Apply using **Claim for Accelerated Benefits SGLV 8284** or **SGLV 8284A** [S1].\n\n4. **Apply for S-DVI**:\n   - You must have a service-connected disability (even if rated at 0%), be in good health (except for service-connected conditions), and apply within 2 years of receiving a new service-connected disability rating [S4].\n\n5. **Contact for Help**:\n   - For SGLI or VGLI: Call **800-419-1473**.\n   - For all other VA life insurance programs: Call **800-669-8477** [S6].\n\nFor more information, visit the VA website or use the VA Life Insurance Center\u2019s resources."
        },
